  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## What's changed\n\nA re-pin release. No managed code in this repository changed, the API is what `11.0.2.2` shipped,\nand the native line is unchanged — MarketingCloudSDK **11.0.2** on iOS, marketingcloudsdk\n**11.0.1** on Android, SFMCSDK **4.0.1** underneath. Both pins that had fallen behind move:\n\n| | was | now |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `MarketingCloudSDK.Net.iOS` | `11.0.2.2` | `11.0.2.3` |\n| `SFMCSDK.Net` | `4.0.1.1` | `4.0.1.2` |\n\n`MarketingCloudSDK.Net.Android` stays at `11.0.1.2`, which is current.\n\n### What the new pins bring\n\n`SFMCSDK.Net 4.0.1.2` is a façade-only revision over the same bindings. It adds **`IsSupported`\nand `IsInitialized`** to `ISfmcSdkClient` — members that answer on every target framework instead\nof throwing, so shared code has something to branch on — and **`NullSfmcSdkClient`**, the no-op\nimplementation for MAUI heads with no SDK and for tests. It also corrects the MAUI\ntarget-framework guidance and states, in both directions, that an app using MobilePush needs only\n*this* package and must never call the core façade's `InitializeAsync`, because the MobilePush\nfaçade already configures the core with its module attached.\n\n`MarketingCloudSDK.Net.iOS 11.0.2.3` is a test-and-documentation revision whose projected API is\nbyte-for-byte `11.0.2.2`'s. It repairs three checks that could not fail — an AppGroupSDK probe\nlooking for a class name that does not exist, an initialization smoke test whose assertion matched\nan inactive stub, and a README-version check blind to the core pin — and fixes a README quick-start\nthat did not compile. Full detail in [its own\nnotes](https://github.com/sbokatuk/MarketingCloudSDK.Net.iOS/blob/HEAD/docs/release-notes/11.0.2.3.md).\n\n### Upgrading from 11.0.2.2\n\n```diff\n-<PackageReference Include=\"MarketingCloudSDK.Net\" Version=\"11.0.2.2\" />\n+<PackageReference Include=\"MarketingCloudSDK.Net\" Version=\"11.0.2.3\" />\n```\n\nNothing to change for callers of `IMarketingCloudClient`, which is unchanged.\n\nOne thing to know if you reach past this façade to the core: **a hand-written fake implementing\n`ISfmcSdkClient` must now add `IsSupported` and `IsInitialized`**, or switch to\n`NullSfmcSdkClient`. `SFMCSDK.Net` is pinned exactly, so this arrives with the upgrade rather than\nwhen you choose it. Fakes of `IMarketingCloudClient` are unaffected.",
